====================================================================================
(1) VALIDATE span-6 {+3,+1,-1,-3}: P = a Z^3 + b Z + c Zbar + d Zbar^3
====================================================================================
  E[P^2] = 2*bc + 12*ad
  E[P^4] = 12*b^2c^2 + 24*b^3d + 24*ac^3 + 576*abcd + 4320*a^2d^2
  E[P^6] = 120*b^3c^3 + 720*b^4cd + 720*abc^4 + 21600*ab^2c^2d + 43200*ab^3d^2 + 43200*a^2c^3d + 907200*a^2bcd^2 + 7257600*a^3d^3
  (death-star: E[P^2]=2bc+12ad ; E[P^6]=...=466560(ad)^3 under E[P^2]=E[P^4]=0)

====================================================================================
(2)/(3) NULLCONE SEARCH (numeric complex) + descent check per stratum
====================================================================================
  span4 {+2,+1,-1,-2} const              depth<= 4, 4000 trials: two-sided nullcone member none (consistent with GMC(2))
  span4 {+2,+1,-1,-2} radial(+R*)        depth<= 8, 4000 trials: two-sided nullcone member none (consistent with GMC(2))
  span6 {+3,+1,-1,-3} const              depth<= 6, 4000 trials: two-sided nullcone member none (consistent with GMC(2))
  span6 {+3,+1,-1,-3} radial             depth<=10, 4000 trials: two-sided nullcone member none (consistent with GMC(2))
  gap>=2 top {+2,+1,-1,-2} vs {+3..}     depth<= 6, 4000 trials: two-sided nullcone member none (consistent with GMC(2))

  => no two-sided nullcone member surfaces; the extreme-charge product is forced nonzero
     (symmetric-top descent). Radial dressing does not open a nullcone at these depths.
